  "slug": "caenorhabditis-element-dynamics-53c3",
  "summary": "Recent preprints and papers refine error modeling in targeted and low-coverage sequencing for repeats, translocations, and epigenetic marks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is quantitative fidelity of sequencing-based readouts of genomic and epigenomic structure. CHARLIE locates interruptions within expanded repeats from Illumina and PacBio targeted sequencing and profiles platform-specific errors, while PASTA applies count-based statistics to quantify and confirm chromosomal translocation junctions from amplicon data. Sparse-Seq shows that low-coverage sequencing can quantify genome-wide 5mC and 5hmC with predictable error, supported by an online error-calculation tool. A rice long-read RNA-seq study finds most plant fusion transcripts are artifacts, mainly RT template switching, and proposes a validation pipeline. Chromatin-focused work extends the theme: 9p21 chromatin topology and distal elements underlie divergent cell-type-specific regulation of p16INK4A, p14ARF and p15INK4B, and nucDetective recovers phased nucleosome arrays in P. falciparum. The shared element is explicit error characterization accompanying each readout.",
